WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.069
Forehand volley for complete beginners. The grip: right hand continental, left hand at the throat.

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:10.405
Ready position: racket face level with your face, ready to protect it.

00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:13.687
In the moving ready position your feet keep bouncing.

00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:19.075
Elbows in front of the body, not tucked in and not stretched out. Knees bent, heels up.

00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:22.853
Unlike at the baseline, you don't make a big turn at the net:

00:00:22.853 --> 00:00:27.560
just turn the body slightly sideways and tilt the racket face back a little.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.001
Keep the elbow and racket face in front of you, never beside or behind your body.

00:00:33.001 --> 00:00:38.374
When you hit, the wrist is cocked and stays firm. Don't chop down with the hand;

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.000 line:10%
Observation area

00:00:38.374 --> 00:00:42.740
move the whole body forward into it, like a wall sliding forward.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:48.241
Lead toward the ball with the butt of the handle instead of dabbing at it with the racket head.

00:00:48.241 --> 00:00:53.800
The left hand pulls inward: elbow to elbow, wrist to wrist, and stamp your left foot as you hit.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.940
Balls at different heights need a different racket face.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.380
The lower the ball, the lower your weight and the more open the racket face.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:06.660
The higher the ball, the taller you stand and the more closed the racket face.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.900
To volley, move diagonally forward to cut off the angle.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.760
Try not to move sideways, or the angle keeps getting wider.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.220
With the basic technique in place, we use the ball machine for volleys on the spot.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.240
Keep the angle small at first so the ball comes right to your hand.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.500
Once you have the right volley feel,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.500
we widen the machine's angle so you have to move diagonally in to cut it off and play the shot.
